  "notes": "Authored from the documented schema; provider terms do not permit redistributing captured data (RIPEstat Service Terms and Conditions, Art. 3.3). Every value in these files is SYNTHETIC: the 40 per-country responses reproduce the envelope and field structure of the live country-resource-stats data call (resolution=1h, starttime=2026-11-09T00:00, run-length encoded `timeline` periods, -1 sentinels for the *_stats fields, occasional fractional hourly aggregates) but the prefix and ASN counts are invented: base levels are a straight line over the watch-list position, with small pseudo-random hourly steps. They are not measurements and say nothing about any country's real routing. To give the diverging layer something to show, invented episodes were written into 2026-11-10: IR −42 % (05:00–10:00 UTC), SD −69 % (from 08:00), MM −20 % (01:00–03:00), CU −88 % (11:00–12:00), KZ +14 % (from 09:00); ET is a hand-written series used by the exact-value test. The files were produced once by a throw-away generator script (not committed) and are static. `capturedAt` is the authoring time. Hourly values run from 2026-11-09T00:00Z to 2026-11-10T15:00Z, which is what the adapter requests at the fixture epoch (48 h before 2026-11-11T00:00Z), so records exist for 2026-11-10 00:00–15:00 UTC. ua.malformed.json is hand-authored (broken entries next to three valid hours).",
